{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"bc9f8e5f-edf0-4810-ad1f-5285b6f88b0d","runId":"0f9f598b-f623-462b-a06c-468496a63682","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":12,"previousEventHash":"sha256:ad6f1b54b6e60e6c9ad90e74c2a781a32fed3940ad654833a588dfe451f627ae","type":"effect.recorded","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04374-f302-7a9e-bc35-0d48ae909598","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:44:30.749Z","idempotencyKey":"effect:github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:147:23cc8f93-c09e-419f-908a-9d05624947a9","payload":{"effectType":"github-label","effectId":"github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:147:23cc8f93-c09e-419f-908a-9d05624947a9","digest":"sha256:a043028dbfe8533441aebaa0bacf945c764c50f8d0b5490423d822716531104f"}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"4ea2e585-dc32-41c8-b427-861c2792571c","runId":"0f9f598b-f623-462b-a06c-468496a63682","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:9d65a643213bc5c122e0e72d769c77c3433850dca2439c0cf6cc6c6f7e0c5e34","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04374-f302-7a9e-bc35-0d48ae909598","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:45:58.433Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":["`src/workflows/work-on.ts:729-787` derives recovery projection from the latest node and maps a started merge to awaiting-merge without consulting durable merge effects.","`src/workflows/work-on.ts:2017-2110` projects a parent merge node as started before reading the current durable run state.","`src/workflows/work-on.ts:2637-2652` records the merge effect, then projects merged, before appending node completion later in the method.","`test/workflows/work-on.test.ts:289-335` covers the pure transition mapping but not preservation of a durable merged stage during restart."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Verdict | **Confirmed** |\n| Confidence | **High** |\n| Severity | **Medium** |\n| Task Type | Recovery correctness bug fix |\n\n## What Was Claimed\n\nAn interrupted orchestrated merge can durably record the merge effect but leave the merge parent node running. On attach, recovery can replace `workflow:merged` with `workflow:awaiting-merge` before subsequent reconciliation succeeds.\n\n## What We Found\n\nThe merge path records its durable `merge` effect and projects the merged label before it appends `node.completed`. The attach path reconstructs the label from the latest node alone, and the resumed parent path projects the merge node's `started` transition before reading durable run state. Both paths therefore map an incomplete merge node to `awaitingMerge`, even when the durable effect already proves the merge succeeded.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nWorkflow-stage derivation treats node status as the only source for label projection. It does not give the irreversible durable merge effect precedence over a stale in-progress merge node.\n\n## Affected Files\n\n- `src/workflows/work-on.ts` — attach reconciliation and parent-node restart projection.\n- `test/workflows/work-on.test.ts` — missing regression coverage for durable merged-stage preservation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/workflows/work-on.ts:729-787` derives recovery projection from the latest node and maps started merge to awaiting-merge.\n- `src/workflows/work-on.ts:2017-2110` projects the parent node's started stage before reading current state.\n- `src/workflows/work-on.ts:2637-2652` persists the merge effect and projects merged before node completion.\n- `test/workflows/work-on.test.ts:289-335` tests only the transition mapper.\n\n## History Findings\n\nIssue #147 was generated from correctness finding `CORRECTNESS-001` on PR #145 for source issue #119. The current integration base includes the merge-effect recording and label lifecycle behavior described by that finding, but no durable-effect precedence guard.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nAdd one deterministic stage-preservation helper that returns `merged` whenever run state contains a durable merge effect. Apply it both while reconciling attach projections and before projecting a resumed parent node's started stage. Add focused tests proving a merge effect overrides awaiting-merge while unrelated effects do not.\n\n## Related Issues\n\n- #119 — source issue for PR #145.\n\n## Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The fix is bounded to one workflow helper, two call sites, and focused unit coverage.\n\n## Acceptance Spec\n\n- [ ] A durable merge effect takes precedence over a stale started merge-node projection.\n- [ ] Attach reconciliation preserves `workflow:merged` after the merge effect is recorded.\n- [ ] Parent-node resume does not project `workflow:awaiting-merge` over durable merge evidence.\n- [ ] Focused regression tests cover merge and non-merge effects.\n- [ ] `npm run check` passes.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->","outputArtifactHash":"investigate-147-confirmed"}}
